# Adds --ids-file to /hai/scratch/yfsun/protenix_sidechain/process.py
#
# That directory is not version controlled, so the change is recorded here.
# process.py hard-coded the weighted before-2021-09-30 index as its only source
# of pdb_ids. The recentPDB eval split is absent from that index by construction
# -- which is exactly what makes the temporal split clean -- so the eval entries
# had no supervision masks and the eval metric could not exclude ambiguous
# residues. This flag lets the same builder run over an arbitrary id list or any
# CSV carrying a pdb_id column. Additive: the default path is unchanged.
#
# Applied with:
#   cd /hai/scratch/yfsun/protenix_sidechain
#   patch -p1 < <this file>
# Then rebuilt the eval masks with:
#   python process.py --ids-file .../recentPDB_low_homology_maxtoken1536.csv \
#       --nproc 32 --out out_eval
#   python make_fampnn.py --in out_eval --out out_eval_fampnn_strictB \
#       --drop-extreme-b
--- a/process.py
+++ b/process.py
